0036:     - Foreground pixels lie on logical rows and columns separated by background spacer rows/columns.
0037:     - A logical row or column is present when it contains at least one foreground pixel.
0038: 
0039:     Rule
0040:     - Expand every background spacer row/column to thickness 2.
0041:     - Expand the logical rows/columns equally so the full output is 26x26.
0042:     - Paint each foreground logical pixel as a solid rectangle of its color.
0043:     - Connect adjacent same-color logical pixels horizontally through the intervening spacer.
0044:     - Connect adjacent same-color logical pixels vertically only when neither endpoint is part of a horizontal same-color run.
0045: 
0046:     Key insight
0047:     - The input is a sampled line drawing: horizontal same-color runs define the bars first, and only unclaimed same-color vertical neighbors are joined.
